3:["$","h2","1",{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"1. Why Humidity Destroys Standard Blinds"}]
4:["$","div","2",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Real wood blinds are the most ",{"children":"Real wood blinds are the most vulnerable to humidity damage. Wood absorbs moisture from the air, causing slats to swell, warp, and eventually crack. The finish can bubble or peel, and trapped moisture creates ideal conditions for mold growth."}],["$","p","Fabric shades face similar ris",{"children":"Fabric shades face similar risks. Natural fibers absorb moisture and can develop musty odors, mildew spots, and structural weakness. Even with regular cleaning, fabric treatments in high-humidity rooms tend to degrade faster than their expected lifespan."}],["$","p","Even metal components aren't i",{"children":"Even metal components aren't immune — steel hardware can rust, and the cords in corded systems can weaken and fray when exposed to persistent moisture."}]]}]
5:["$","h2","3",{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"2. Best Materials for Wet Environments"}]
6:["$","div","4",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Faux wood blinds top the list ",{"children":"Faux wood blinds top the list for high-humidity rooms. Made from PVC or composite materials, they're completely impervious to moisture. Modern faux wood options are nearly indistinguishable from real wood, offering the same warmth and elegance without the vulnerability."}],["$","p","Aluminum blinds are another ex",{"children":"Aluminum blinds are another excellent choice — lightweight, rust-resistant, and available in a wide range of finishes. They're particularly well-suited for kitchens where grease and steam are constant companions."}],["$","p","For a softer look, consider vi",{"children":"For a softer look, consider vinyl roller shades or polyester cellular shades. Both resist moisture absorption and can be wiped clean easily. Cellular shades also provide insulation, helping to regulate the temperature swings common in humid rooms."}]]}]
7:["$","div","5",{"className":"rounded-lg bg-ice p-6","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[15px] font-semibold leading-[27.2px] tracking-[0.56px] text-navy","children":"The best window treatment for a humid room is one that looks great on day one and still looks great after a year of daily showers, cooking steam, or Florida rain blowing through an open window."}]}]
8:["$","h2","6",{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"3. Ventilation and Installation Tips"}]
9:["$","div","7",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Even with moisture-resistant m",{"children":"Even with moisture-resistant materials, proper ventilation extends the life of your window treatments. Ensure bathroom exhaust fans are running during and after showers. In kitchens, use range hoods to redirect steam away from nearby windows."}],["$","p","Mount blinds with enough clear",{"children":"Mount blinds with enough clearance from the window glass to allow air circulation behind them. Condensation on window glass is common in air-conditioned Florida homes, and trapped moisture between glass and blinds accelerates any potential issues."}],["$","p","Consider outside-mount install",{"children":"Consider outside-mount installations in humid rooms. This allows more airflow around the treatment and makes cleaning easier — simply lift the blinds away from the window for a thorough wipe-down."}]]}]
